  "summary_en": "Saudi Arabia's SDAIA AI Ethics Principles and Controls (May 2025) set seven principles (fairness, privacy and security, humanity, social and environmental benefits, reliability and safety, transparency, accountability) applied across the AI lifecycle, with a four-tier risk classification, roles, optional registration, badges, tools and checklists. Embodied AI appears only in passing, for example autonomous vehicles.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Seven AI ethics principles with controls at each AI lifecycle stage: plan, data, build, deploy.",
   "Four risk tiers; high-risk systems need conformity assessments and unacceptable-risk systems (social profiling, child exploitation) are banned.",
   "Human oversight is required for irreversible or life-and-death decisions; no social scoring or mass surveillance.",
   "SDAIA monitors compliance; entities appoint CDO, compliance officer and Responsible AI Officer; registration and badges are optional.",
   "Annexes provide ethics tools and a checklist, with some items binding on third parties."
  ],
